    "applicability": {
      "scope": "Interpret Ascend CANN profiling evidence from step breakdown through kernel/utilization/communication analysis, and assess execution/validator evidence in automated optimization-stage reports.",
      "prerequisites": "Usable warm-state captures with representative steps, required files and non-null utilization columns; healthy cards and a consistent valid topology for multi-card comparisons.",
      "input_contract": "CANN step/kernel/utilization/communication outputs with verified column semantics; for stage acceptance, the loaded candidate, baseline, quality-validator output and comparable measurements.",
      "produced_artifact": "An evidence-qualified bottleneck classification and optimization direction; stage conclusions retain missing-execution/validator INCONCLUSIVE or observed gate-failure FAIL.",
      "failure_modes": "Summing concurrent communication durations double-counts overlap; misidentified columns can drop communication, and a successful export can still lack usable utilization data."
    },
    "state": "candidate",
    "limitations": [
      "Source-derived candidate; no local efficacy validation.",
      "Original typed source inventory is not normalized; retain source identities and limits in the procedure/readsets.",
      "The CannBot stage and MindStudio service readsets identify their respective sources. Inherited MindIE-SD guidance retains its historical attribution.",
      "CannBot callback predicates do not establish numerical accuracy or performance; dependent skills, agent-host integration and NPU execution are unverified.",
      "Checkout-only local skill; no automatic execution or promotion.",
